>
	<p>
		I am an electrical engineer who lives in the Greater Cleveland area. Currently I work as a test engineer, where I design, implement, program, and maintain automated test systems for our production facilities. This is an exciting role, where I
		have the opportunity to work with a wide variety of technologies, from PLCs, high level programming languages like C# and C++, and electrical schematic design. In addition to the technologies I work with, I have had a fantastic opportunity to lead projects, 
		where I can take on a leadership role, and work with a great team comprised of people from all over the world. 
		
	</p>

	<p>
		When I was studying for my M.S. in Electrical Engineering, I worked as a graduate research assistant, where I researched and developed a novel method for detecting and classifying faults in electrical power systems using machine learning techniques. 
		This project ignited a great interest in machine learning, and I have continued to learn about this field. Additionally, during these studies, I was a graduate teaching assistant, where I found teaching undergraduate students Embedded Systems Programming 
		and Digital Logic Design to be a very rewarding experience. 

	</p>
	
	<p>
		In my free time, I enjoy working on personal projects, learning about new technologies, exploring Cleveland, riding bikes, taking photos, and going to concerts with my friends.
	</p>

